  "methodology": "FMV builds bottoms-up by mapping FPI's ~71.6K post-disposition acres to nine state / quality buckets and applying USDA NASS 2024 Land Values Summary state averages plus Iowa State and other survey premiums for Class-A ground. The largest single assumption is that ~22K acres of central-Illinois / Iowa-Class-A / central-Nebraska ground deserves a premium over USDA averages — this is consistent with Iowa State's CARD survey which prices top-quality Iowa ground at $13,200/acre vs. the $11,150 NASS state average. Implied NAV/share at FMV deducts net debt (debt + Series A pref RNCI − cash) and divides by current diluted shares. FPI trades closer to its book value per acre than LAND because the portfolio is mostly Midwest row-crop where state-average values track book more tightly than California permanent crops."
